Package: lor-i2s-dkms
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Light-O-Rama <unknown@example.com>
Depends: dkms (>= 3), linux-headers-rpi-2712, kmod
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: Patched RP1 DesignWare I2S driver for the HiFiBerry DAC (DKMS)
 Fixes "Invalid argument" when opening the HiFiBerry DAC (pcm5102a) on
 CM5/Pi 5: the DWC I2S driver never sets runtime->hw.info, so on RP1's
 non-coherent DMA snd_pcm_open_substream builds an empty access mask and
 fails with EINVAL. This package adds SNDRV_PCM_INFO_INTERLEAVED in
 dw_i2s_startup(). DKMS rebuilds designware_i2s.ko for every new kernel, so
 the fix survives kernel upgrades. Removes earlier hand-installed
 dpkg-diverted copies of the module.
